VALUES
  ('utrecht-2026-top32-robin-rocks','utrecht-eu-finals-2026','Top 32',3,'OP09-062','Purple/Yellow Nico Robin','GW12','OP17-039','Blue Rocks.D.Xebec','Blank',0,1,'OP17-039',2,1,1,'Game 1: Rocks (Blank) wins. Rocks chooses to go first and develops Kill, Newgate, and Gloriosa while drawing and filtering with the leader. Robin (GW12) develops Pudding and Yamato, ramps to 10 DON, and plays Big Mom for life gain and trigger bodies. Rocks controls the board with Gloriosa, Shiki, Newgate, and Kaido, shrinking and removing a rested Big Mom before building a board of 10-cost Rocks, Newgate, and Shiki. Robin cannot keep pace with the large attacks, and Rocks takes the game.

Game 2 — Unfinished: Robin chooses to go first, ramps with Yamato and the leader, and reaches another Big Mom. Perospero and Sweet 3 Generals pressure Rocks’ board while Rocks draws through the leader and Linlin, then rebuilds with Rocks, Shiki, Newgate, and Stussy. Robin leads in life, while Rocks has more cards and board presence. The game is still in progress when time is called. Rocks is already ahead 1–0, so the event overtime ruling awards the match to Rocks. Game 2 has no winner.','User-provided match summary','https://onepiece.gg/championship-26-27-finals/','VERIFIED');
